## Portfolio decision

Block32 is meaningful program progress because it closes the guarded finite
factor-channel bridge and removes a plausible selector from the priority
stack.  It does not produce a retained end-to-end theory, retire an obligation,
or justify a lane-percentage change.

The next campaign is the common-dilation/shared-cause resource locus, not the
large NN validator/compiler.  It must distinguish three possibilities:

1. one fixed interaction and physically supplied environment select a proper
   subset of `[0,1)`;
2. the full interval survives only by varying an unowned environment state,
   localizing the missing physical ownership theorem; or
3. exact third-use renewal fails or forces growing history, localizing the
   autonomous resource obstruction.

In parallel, the pair-sensitive conserved-source contraction is the strongest
independent route because it reads the nonzero tensor that all one-tip additive
tests miss.  If neither route can be obtained from the approved primitives or
existing physical carriers, that is the point at which an axiom-interface
proposal becomes evidence-driven.  Block32 itself does not indicate an axiom
